ar values of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404773 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5bd4cb7d-93c2-588f-99ae-34346d7bdefb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404773 #edb/ref 1074 "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nFirst, we calculate ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the characteristic equation of ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{A}^{T}\\,A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )(2-\\lambda )-4 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda  & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (\\lambda -4) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =4,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{4}=2 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404774 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404775 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404774 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404776 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404774 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404777 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404774 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404778 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404774 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404779 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404774 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404774 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404774 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186404775 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404774 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "9eed5c36-5d57-5b08-a6c1-2725fe122f8a" #edb/ref 1759